      "risk_7d": "10% LOW",
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "Western and Central Atlantic (AL94):\nA non-tropical low pressure area located several hundred miles \nsouth-southeast of Bermuda is producing disorganized showers and \nthunderstorms. The low could still acquire some subtropical \ncharacteristics through tonight before upper-level winds increase \non Sunday. The low is forecast to move generally eastward over the \nwestern and central subtropical Atlantic during the next couple of \ndays and become absorbed by a new non-tropical low pressure system \nto its east early next week. Regardless, gale-force winds are \nlikely over parts of the central subtropical Atlantic through the \nweekend. For more information, including Gale Warnings, see High \nSeas Forecasts issued by the National Weather Service.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...low...10 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...low...10 percent.",
      "metadata": {
        "chance_48h_level": "LOW",
