      "platform_location": "13.6S 54.3E",
      "wind": "25-30 kt",
      "risk_48h": null,
      "risk_7d": null,
      "next_update": null,
      "raw_text": "(1) THE AREA OF CONVECTION (INVEST 94S) PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR \n13.6S 55.4E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 13.6S 54.3E, APPROXIMATELY 392 NM \nNORTHEAST OF TOAMASINA, MADAGASCAR. ANIMATED MULTISPECTRAL SATELLITE \nIMAGERY (MSI) AND A 070331Z 91 GHZ MICROWAVE IMAGE DEPICT A \nCONSOLIDATING LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC), WITH DEVELOPING \nCENTRAL CONVECTION. ELEVATED WINDS ALONG THE SOUTHERN PERIPHERY \nINDICATE A MORE FAVORABLE CHANCE OF DEVELOPMENT AS SEEN IN A 070435Z \nMETOP-B ASCAT PASS. ENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS DEPICTS A MARGINALLY \nFAVORABLE ENVIRONMENT WITH WARM SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES OF 29-30C, \nLOW TO MODERATE VERTICAL WIND SHEAR OF 15-20 KTS, AND GOOD POLEWARD \nOUTFLOW ALOFT. GLOBAL ENSEMBLE MODELS ARE IN AGREEANCE WITH 94S \nTRANSITING SLOWLY WESTWARD. GLOBAL DETERMINISTIC MODELS WITH THE \nEXCEPTION OF ECMWF ARE REMAINING CONSERVATIVE WITH MINIMAL DEVELOPMENT \nBEFORE MAKING LANDFALL OVER NORTHERN MADAGASCAR. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED \nSURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 25 TO 30 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL \nPRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1000 MB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE \nDEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS \nIS UPGRADED TO HIGH. SEE REF A (WTXS21 PGTW 070630) FOR FURTHER \nDETAILS.",
